      "id": "1-timeline-architecture-execution-mechanics",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "1. Timeline Architecture & Execution Mechanics"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Retiam's animation system is built around asynchronous timeline promises, deterministic clock stepping, and declarative motion choreography."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "mermaid",
          "code": "flowchart TD\n  S[\"Scene timeline<br/>scene.play / scene.wait\"] --> A[\"Atomic animations<br/>Create / FadeIn / MoveTo\"]\n  S --> C[\"Concurrent animations<br/>ScatterAssemble / CascadeIn\"]\n  S --> Q[\"Sequential animations<br/>Serial choreography\"]\n  A --> AT[\"Animator.ts<br/>Progress alpha with Rate.ts easing\"]\n  C --> CT[\"Concurrent.ts<br/>Per-child stagger using lagRatio\"]\n  Q --> QT[\"Sequential.ts<br/>Zero-gap dt handoff to queued children\"]\n  AT --> U[\"State updates<br/>Transforms, paints, stencil and geometries\"]\n  CT --> U\n  QT --> U"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "variant": "info",
          "content": "For in-depth architectural specifications on serial and concurrent orchestration, composite hierarchies, proportional time scaling, and completion-boundary handoffs, see [`SEQUENTIAL_AND_CONCURRENT_ANIMATION_ARCHITECTURE.md`](/notes-sequential-and-concurrent-animation-architecture)."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 4,
          "text": "Rate & Easing Mechanics ([Rate.ts](../src/engine/animation/Rate.ts))"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Every animation samples progress $t \\in [0, 1]$ through configurable easing curves:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "`linear`: Constant speed.",
            "`smooth`: Standard cubic ease-in-out ($3t^2 - 2t^3$).",
            "`easeInOutCubic`: Steeper cubic transition.",
            "`rushInto` / `rushFrom`: Rapid acceleration or deceleration.",
            "`doubleSmooth`: Quintic polynomial with zero first and second derivatives at endpoints.",
            "`wiggle(n)`: Sinusoidal oscillation around target value.",
            "`thereAndBack`: Ping-pong curve reaching $1.0$ at $t = 0.5$ and returning to $0.0$ at $t = 1.0$.",
            "`spring({ damping, stiffness, mass })`: Physically accurate damped harmonic oscillator simulation."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
